    "explanation": "To the rider: I can see why the charge feels unfair, but the evidence does not support the account that the driver never came, and the fee stands. To the driver: the record supports your arrival and your wait, and you are compensated for it. What the record establishes: EV-GPS-00208 is the driver's own trace, unbroken at 10-second intervals with 100% coverage and no gaps. It places him inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 16:02:10 — 15 seconds before his 16:02:25 'arrived' marker — with 60 qualifying in-radius fixes and a closest approach of 28.8 m to the pin. He then held position continuously for 585 seconds, to 16:11:55, which is 285 seconds more than the 300-second free waiting period in force for this trip (EV-TRIP-00208 platform policy). The trip was terminated by him at 16:12:10 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, which POL-NS-01(d) recognises, with no boarding recorded. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold. Why the rider's own routes do not run: her device (EV-GPS-00208) sits stationary 633–646 m from the pickup pin across the whole window, never inside the 150 m rider-presence radius, so it does not support a 15-minute wait at the guardhouse. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her because the driver replied in the chat 18 seconds after her 16:08:02 message and made an answered 34-second in-app call at 16:09:40 — limb (b) is not met. POL-NS-05 is not triggered: the driver was stationary in-geofence at the marker, not 300 m away or moving at 15 km/h. POL-NS-06 has nothing to correct: there is a 285-second surplus, not a shortfall. POL-NS-03 does not apply, because the driver's fixes were inside the radius, not outside it. The POL-NS-01 'in-radius → FULL_REFUND' argument is rejected: that sentence addresses the case where the driver has himself recorded DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, his own admission that he could not find the rider, and the clause's note confirms its FULL_REFUND is licensed only on that in-radius DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE outcome. This driver used RIDER_NO_SHOW, a code limb (d) expressly recognises, so that sentence and its 'mis-selected reason code' referral have no application. Integrity: nothing is impaired under POL-NS-08 — 100% coverage, a 0.0 s maximum gap, the expected 10 s cadence, all six chat messages the trip record counts, and an SGD 8.00 fare line equal to the platform figure, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. EV-ADVIS-00208-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), but no finding rests on it: the single 585-second run clears the minimum on its own. The outcome: the SGD 8.00 cancellation fee stands and is not refunded. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is paid 80% of the fee — SGD 6.40 — the residual 20% being retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below the 4 required) and 2 ÷ 143 completed trips is 0.014 (below 0.08). The ruling is therefore DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and per POL-GEN-03 amount_sgd carries the same SGD 6.40 as driver_compensation_sgd; the SGD 8.00 charge stands. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires — there is no repeat dispute between these parties, no anti-farming pattern, and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 1 — so the fallback request for escalation is refused, the clauses having licensed an outcome. The monetary effect (SGD 6.40) is at or below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04. On the profiles: the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter (3), the rating, the cancellation rate and the prior disputes filed are context only under POL-GEN-01, and nothing here rests on them. Finally, the rider's request that someone call her is noted: her separate right to have the dispute decided by a person, outside this ruling, is preserved under POL-GEN-08(3), and the appeal route is hers under POL-GEN-04."
